text:
alex_k: Quick heads-up — we're planning a change to the partner batch endpoint shape that will be a breaking change for older SDKs. Need partner sync and a rollout plan.

mira_s: Ugh ok — what's changing exactly?

alex_k: Current payload: ```{
  "requests": [{ "input": "...", "metadata": {} }],
  "options": {}
}``` New payload will require `content` instead of `input`, add an optional `attachments` array, and move per-request metadata into `request_meta`. Example: ```{
  "requests": [{ "content": "...", "request_meta": {}, "attachments": [] }],
  "options": {}
}```

jordan_pm: Why the rename? backwards-incompatibility is a heavy lift for partners.

alex_k: Two reasons: 1) alignment with our streaming wire format (we standardized on `content`) and 2) attachments enable structured multimodal batching (we need the shape to support reference blobs).

sam_ops: Timeline? We should give partners a clear window and a compatibility shim.

alex_k: Proposal: 90-day deprecation window + compatibility shim in the hosted layer for 120 days. During the window, both payload shapes accepted, but we'll log warnings and emit header `X-RW-Deprecated: batch-input` when old shape used. After 90 days, return 400 for new writes, continue read-compat for 30 days.

tina_partner: From partner side: market SDKs will need a patch release. Can we provide a strict JSON schema + sample fixtures and a dockerized test harness?

mira_s: Yes, we should provide: 1) JSON schemas (old/new), 2) open-source shim patch for node/python, 3) integration tests that run in CI, and 4) a staging canary partner list.

alex_k: Agreed. Owners: SDK shims — @mira_s, Test harness + fixtures — @jordan_pm, Canary rollout coord — @sam_ops, Partner comms — @tina_partner.

jordan_pm: Canary plan: 2 weeks internal canary, then 1 week partner canary with 3 partners (marketplace vendor, SI, and HW partner) flagged in console. If no regressions, gradual ramp over 2 weeks.

alex_k: Messaging: will send an initial "intent to change" notice today, followed by formal deprecation notice in 7 days with migration guide and code samples. Then reminders at 30/60/15 days before enforcement.

sam_ops: Operational hooks: able to toggle shim per-tenant (feature flag), activate stricter validation on a percentage, and automated rollback if error rate delta >3% or 5xx spike. Add SLO check for latency regressions too.

release-bot: Deploy scheduled: staging: 2026-07-08T10:00:00Z, canary: 2026-07-22T02:00:00Z, enforcement: 2026-10-20T00:00:00Z.

tina_partner: Partners asked for an RFC board / doc where they can comment — can we share a short-form Google doc + migration checklist?

mira_s: I'll create the checklist and examples today. Will include quickpatch snippets: Node example: ```js
// shim example (node)
function normalizeBatch(payload){
  if(payload.requests && payload.requests[0] && payload.requests[0].input){
    payload.requests = payload.requests.map(r => ({...r, content: r.input, request_meta: r.metadata || {}}));
  }
  return payload;
}
```

alex_k: Good. Also let's add a lightweight e2e test: send both shapes -> expect identical downstream record. jordan_pm can add to harness.

jordan_pm: Will do. I'll add the following test cases: old-only, new-only, mixed in same batch, attachments present.

sam_ops: For marketplace listings: we need to flag SDK compatibility in vendor docs and add a migration notice banner in the console for affected partners. ops will own console banner.

tina_partner: I can coordinate partner comms and collect partner-specific constraints (e.g., long release cycles for some SI vendors). Please add a column in the partner tracking sheet for "release freeze windows".

alex_k: Action items summary (short):
- mira_s: SDK shim repos + node/python examples (ETA 3 days)
- jordan_pm: test harness + e2e cases (ETA 5 days)
- sam_ops: feature flag + console banner + canary infra (ETA 1 week)
- tina_partner: partner comms + collect release windows (ETA 2 days)
- alex_k: deprecation calendar + release PRs + extra monitoring hooks (ETA 2 days)

tina_partner: SGTM, I'll start scheduling partner office hours for migration support.

mira_s: Will open the SDK shim repos and link them in the doc.

alex_k: Thanks all. If anyone needs to be added to the partner canary list, ping me and include org ID. We'll keep tickets lightweight — prefer PRs against the shared migration doc. :thumbsup:
